# The background display exists only while an agent works in the background (Boss, 2026-10-26: "it should only
# flip on when we're using it"): Robinhood refused to run beside the always-on display, and FFIV Companion drew its
# touch screen on it. The helper (tools/background-display/SomaDisplay.java) makes it when Soma asks before a
# background step and lets it go 2 minutes after the last ask. Real displays, real apps: phone only.
[phone] With no agent working in the background, `adb shell dumpsys display | grep -c soma-agent` says 0, and `oma-phone status` still says backgroundAvailable true (the helper is up, no display).
[phone] `oma-phone --display bg open settings:display --until Display` works: the display is made for it (backgroundDisplayId appears in status) and the main screen never changes.
[phone] Two minutes after the last background step, soma-agent is gone again (dumpsys count 0).
[phone] Robinhood opens and works with no "screen recording" warning while no background step has run for two minutes.
[phone] FFIV Companion shows both DS screens on the main screen.
[phone] A background step while Robinhood is open in front: the step runs on the hidden display; note whether Robinhood complains (expected: it may, while the display is up).

# Focus regression: run only awake/unlocked, with Boss's agreement to use the composer.
# Do not submit, clear or replace his draft. Do not unlock or enable permissions.
[phone] On the old helper, focus Soma's main-screen composer with the keyboard visible; record dumpsys window mTopFocusedDisplayId and dumpsys input_method focused/served client and input visibility. Launch a harmless URL on bg in a browser not used on main; record whether the IME disappears and whether top focus leaves display 0. If unavailable, mark reproduction NOT RUN.
[phone] After deploying rebuilt helper with STEAL_TOP_FOCUS_DISABLED and recreating its display, focus the main-screen Soma composer again. Run oma-phone --display bg url https://example.com --app com.brave.browser (about:blank is invalid and proves nothing), then bg screen and a harmless bg press/scroll. With the launch guard installed expect the URL to return waiting:true, reason:boss-typing, actionMayHaveRun:false without launching. Check after each step: mTopFocusedDisplayId remains 0, main composer retains input focus, keyboard stays visible with the same IME client, draft unchanged. Do not send text.
[phone] Repeat with the bg browser already running and after its two-minute idle release/new display creation; main keyboard and focus remain unchanged throughout. Verify bg controls and screenshot still work; no main-screen restore/tap is used.
[phone] Owner-only Take over still moves the bg task onto main deliberately, after pausing, as before. Mark separately from the no-focus-steal assertions.

[phone] Before focus retest, with Boss-provided Wi-Fi/ADB: record running SomaDisplay PID/CLASSPATH, deployed soma-display.dex SHA256, dumpsys display FLAGS, window top-focused display and input_method served/focused client. Compare the dex to 56b75ca1 checkpoint, repeat after idle close/recreate and healer restart. If unavailable, mark identity/flags NOT VERIFIED rather than assuming the deployed path proves loaded bytes.
[phone] With main Soma composer and IME visible, test both bg open settings:display and bg url https://example.com: each returns the explicit waiting: Boss is typing non-success and neither launches nor replaces the previous opened-app guard. Repeat with the helper display idle/released; direct open/url must defer before creating a display. Existing bg screen/press/screenshot can still run under their normal access rules; verify main draft, IME and input client remain unchanged. After Boss closes IME, retry open/url and verify they launch on bg, never main. No automated IME dismissal or send.
[phone] With a bg plan whose next step opens a URL, show the main IME before that step: the launch step must fail with waiting/boss-typing in its result, no activity launch, and a retained receipt. Read that receipt rather than replaying the plan under a fresh id.
